<mxCell id="c45" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules of thumb&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#545B64;fillColor=#FFFFFF;dashed=0;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="770" y="630" width="690" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c46" value="1. Limits come from the tier config, not from code. Changing a tier is a config push.&lt;br&gt;2. The tenant id used for limits comes from the authorizer, never from a header&lt;br&gt;    the client sets. Otherwise one tenant can spend another tenant's budget.&lt;br&gt;3. A big tenant is allowed to be slower. It is never allowed to make others slower.&lt;br&gt;4. Bulk and interactive work never share a queue or a worker pool.&lt;br&gt;5. If one tenant is consistently above 25% of a shared resource, that is a&lt;br&gt;    sales conversation about a bigger tier or a silo, not an ops ticket." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;fontColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=0;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="790" y="665" width="660" height="121" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
